{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1103098-bruja-2e-conversion","id":1103098,"title":"Bruja [2E Conversion]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T06:11:26-07:00","id":1103098,"title":"Bruja [2E Conversion]","content":"Like with the Dead Wolves, this is a Bruja conversion for second edition and the Chronicles of Darkness, using the Gift/Bane + 4 Devotions scheme. These Devotions are pretty cheap because their use is usually highly situational, but we chose these because they were particularly cool in theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Bruja</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animalism, Protean, Resilience, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Vigor</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Gift: Brother Beatdown</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Any time a Bruja enters combat, they gain +1 to attack rolls for every additional Bruja involved in the same combat, even if it's just two Bruja against each other (+1 for each), up to a maximum of +5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bane</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Bruja are ever hungry, and always walking a fine line of losing control. Penalties from Hunger and Starvation apply to all actions, not just frenzy resistance. Additionally, Bruja may never control or direct a Hunger Frenzy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Devotions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Curbstomp (Vigor 2)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bruja understand that armor alone can't protect you. A Bruja with this Devotion adds an active power to their Vigor Discipline allowing them to spend 1 Vitae to ignore any and all mundane armor an opponent is wearing for an attack.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curbstomp costs 1 Experience.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Dayrider (Resilience 2, Protean 1)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Bruja rides until he reaches his destination, heedless of any hindrance, even the sun itself. As long as the Bruja continues to ride a motorcycle, they ignore damage from sunlight (and only sunlight) for a number of hours up to their Humanity. This costs one vitae per hour, and does not negate the possibility of fear frenzy - many Bruja will succumb immediately upon reaching a destination if they do not plan ahead. Dayrider cannot be activated again until the Bruja sleeps in their Unmarked Grave.</span></span> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dayrider costs 2 Experiences.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Feed the Hog! (Vigor 2, Resilience 2, Animalism 1)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Bruja's ride is their kin. With this Devotion, the Bruja can mix their Vitae into the fuel tank. For as long as that fuel lasts, the vehicle doubles its top and safe speeds, and adds the Bruja's Resilience to its Structure (allowing it to survive the gruesome pressures of traveling at those speeds). A minimum of 3 points of Vitae must be mixed into a full tank of fuel, and the tank cannot be refilled until it is completely empty.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feed the Hog! costs 2 Experiences.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Blood-Soaked Leather (Vigor 1 OR Resilience 1)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bruja have to be able to protect their own. This Devotion allows a Bruja to bestow their awesome physical might unto their human ghouls and thralls. By coating their own leather biker jackets in their Vitae, they can grant the use of either their Vigor or Resilience (or both, if both versions of the Devotion are learned and paid for) to a ghoul or thrall for a scene. The Bruja must spend at least 1 Vitae on coating the leather jacket, but may spend more, and the recipient of the leather jacket may spend that Vitae to use the active effects of the Discipline imparted. The Bruja must also be the one that puts the jacket on the subject in a pseudo-ceremonial moment. The Bruja loses access to the Discipline during the scene in which the recipient wears the jacket.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blood-Soaked Leather costs 1 Experience, and may be bought twice, each representing either Vigor or Resilience.</span></span> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T15:06:25-07:00","id":1103297,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about Dayrider. On one hand, it is thematic and awesome. On the other, Sunlight is a pretty major deal and a pack of thugs circumventing it sends my inner Invictus Elder crazy. And truthfully, I am siding with my crazy Elder.<br /> <br /> As for the Gift: it makes fights more lethal. It does so in proportion to Bruja presence and works even if two are fighting. With it, bar brawls may have just become a ticket to torpor. As such, the real life reaction would be to tone down intra-bloodline fighting (via 'honor' or what have you) to avoid most bloodline members going splat. That ups the 'close-knit group' theme but downplays the 'chaos and mayhem' theme. Your call if that is bad or good, or if I am even right. I am just mentioning it because it is where my mind went.<br /> <br /> I LOVE feed the hog, curbstomp, and blood-soaked leather. Fast bikes, brutal beatings, and initiation-by-jacket. Good calls.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:15:52-07:00","id":1103317,"title":"","content":"I think Dayrider adding the Ascendant Coil, making Ordo Bruja (<a href=\"http://www.thelibraryofmyth.com/uploads/5/8/1/6/58166339/f01_-_vampire_the_requiem_-_count_f-cking_dracula.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Count F**King Dracula</a> comes to mind) terrifying to the aforementioned Elders would be more balanced. Maybe having a Devotion attuned to each Covenant, show casing the bloodline's diverse branches. Bikers are a continental US phenomena so being diverse makes sense. It's a big area, plenty of room for different groups.<br /> <br /> I think this approach adds a bit of balance that makes such an amazing power both more plausible in setting but no less special, and a great excuse to come up with other nifty powers exclusive to other covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-13-2017, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:27:12-07:00","id":1104011,"title":"","content":"I like Dayrider as a scale for the Ascendant Coil. Seems more plausible then. Ties into riding as an expression of freedom from limits too, so that's nifty.<br /> <br /> To throw in some ideas for the other covenants:<br /> <br /> The Lance could have a group Theban ritual where the Bruja become a crusading army, and ride to the 'Holy Land with God's protection'. So high level group ritual that makes it less about the Journey and more about the destination. Riding into the Sun and such.<br /> <br /> The Carthians could have something similar. Based on Carthian law and the idea of exporting the revolution, when the Carthian's take power (an act that depends upon context but which must be viewed as legitimate nevertheless), then those with the devotion can bring the Revolution to new lands. Ties to the theme of blazing a trail and, given the rarity of its use, would justify a Majesty-like boost when you get there. Heck, make it a contagion power, where the boost disrupts the local power structure by giving the local oppressed a new boon but the Bruja cannot stick around, and must keep riding. As such, they also act to sow fear throughout a region as their arrival means trouble.<br /> <br /> The Invictus have the Oaths and a tradition of Elders preferring messagers over tech but I feel that pursuing that line is too counter to the Bruja. However, I suppose if there was such an Invictus Bruja, braving the road as a representative of his Lord might work.<br /> <br /> I am drawing a blank on the Crone but I know it needs to be connected to the idea of the bike as a living mount and the vampire as a badass. The ritual would need a ton of blood too. Maybe a 'hunting the roads' kind of stick, which departs from the others in that the road is the destination. The Crone isn't going anyway; it is going nowhere fast.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T02:02:09-07:00","id":1104201,"title":"","content":"Curbstomp should probably only ignore a number of points of armour up to your ranks in Vigor.<br /> Dayrider is getting Coil of the Ascendant on the cheap and I wouldn't allow it in my games.<br /> Feed The Hog grants a big increase in speed without any ranks in Celerity, I would change how it works.<br /> Blood-Soaked Leather seems mostly fine, there does seem to be a trend in 2e that Vigor is used to &quot;push&quot; Disciplines onto other people so it might make sense to cost it at (Vigor 2 Resilience 1 or Vigor 1 Resilience 2) instead so it takes some ability with the Discipline to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T03:29:18-07:00","id":1104212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1103098-bruja-2e-conversion?p=1104201#post1104201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curbstomp should probably only ignore a number of points of armour up to your ranks in Vigor.<br /> Dayrider is getting Coil of the Ascendant on the cheap and I wouldn't allow it in my games.<br /> Feed The Hog grants a big increase in speed without any ranks in Celerity, I would change how it works.<br /> Blood-Soaked Leather seems mostly fine, there does seem to be a trend in 2e that Vigor is used to &quot;push&quot; Disciplines onto other people so it might make sense to cost it at (Vigor 2 Resilience 1 or Vigor 1 Resilience 2) instead so it takes some ability with the Discipline to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of these I concur with. Except the Coil of the Ascendant comment. I don't care about devotions imitating portions of coils and scales because most coils just look like a bunch of devotions lumped together into a grab bag with a theme tag on the handle and given a massive price break by not having any discipline or devotion prerequisites and an additional covenant advantage of being eligible for additional price breaks to lower the cost down to 1 xp per power.<br /> I have more issue with the fact that a just out of the box embraced Bruja can buy every power except Feed the Hog and that none of them tie into the bloodline gift. I'd personally up the discipline requirements to Animalism 2 (which is where they can make Energizer zombies) for Feed the Hog and actually incorporate their bloodline gift as a requirement to activating most of them. (Maybe they require a fellow Bruja with them to enhance their ride or at least one to witness the jacket ceremony.)<br /> By the way, what happens if the thrall loses the jacket or the Bruja's ride gets taken. For example, they get stopped and dominated or majestied into handing over their jacket or vehicle (yes, I noticed it is worded to be technically applicable to cars, boats, planes, trains etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T04:04:40-07:00","id":1104221,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing this conversion here. Could you just please don't forget to link to the original post next time? <a href=\"http://reno.mechanipus.com/wiki/Bruja\" target=\"_blank\">http://reno.mechanipus.com/wiki/Bruja</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}